---
slug: support/inbound/sendgrid(/:token)
method: post
format: json
layout: ''
---
{%- comment -%}
  SendGrid Inbound Parse posts here, in raw mode: the whole message
  arrives as the text field `email`, with the delivery `envelope` beside
  it. The secret is part of the URL, either as the trailing path segment
  or as ?token=, because Inbound Parse does not sign its requests.

  Raw mode is not a preference. In the provider's parsed mode attachments
  arrive as Rails upload objects that Liquid cannot touch, and the
  message cannot be read at all once one is present.

  The work is done inline. SendGrid wants a prompt 2xx, and if this ever
  grows slow enough to matter the body of it moves to a background job and
  this page keeps answering straight away.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  comment
    Every arrival is logged before the secret is checked, and that is the
    point of it: a refused post writes nothing anywhere else, so without
    this line "the provider never called us" and "the provider called us
    and we said no" look identical from the outside. Inbound Parse keeps
    no log of its own at the provider, so this is the only record that an
    email reached the door.

    The delivery envelope only: who sent it and where it was addressed,
    both small and both already known to the provider. Not the token,
    which would put the endpoint's whole authentication in the log, and
    not the message, which is the customer's.
  endcomment
  log context.params.envelope, type: 'modules/support/inbound: a post arrived'

  comment
    Named keys only, never the params hash itself. In the provider's
    parsed mode a posted file arrives as a Rails object with no Liquid
    representation, and touching the hash as a whole, passing it on
    included, raises before anything can run. Raw mode avoids the file
    parts entirely, and reading one key at a time keeps it safe either
    way.
  endcomment
  function neutral = 'modules/support/helpers/email/from_raw', raw: context.params.email, envelope: context.params.envelope, token: context.params.token

  function result = 'modules/support/commands/inbound/receive', params: neutral

  assign status = result.status | default: 200
  if status != 200
    response_status status
  endif

  assign body = { "ok": result.ok, "error": result.error, "ticket_number": result.ticket_number, "new_ticket": result.new_ticket, "reopened": result.reopened }
  echo body | json
-%}
